<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălyzĭa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ălyzēa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλυζία</span>, Thuc.
		and Strabo; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλύζεια</span>, Steph. Byz.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in
				Acarnania with a temple dedicated to Hercules</i>, now <i>Kandili</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad Alyziam accesseramus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 16, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acarnanum urbes, Alyzia, Stratos etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 4,
					1, 2, § 5</span></i>
			; cf. Mann. Greece, 76 and 77.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
